{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.591 acc, showing multiprofile RNA is a strong direction. However, we only know multimodal helps in the singleprofile setting (config_016: 0.527 vs config_001: 0.485, +4.2 pts), and image-only is very weak (0.208), raising uncertainty about whether the image signal adds value or noise when combined with the already-strong multiprofile RNA. Question: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests whether adding the image modality improves upon the best-performing RNA-only multiprofile baseline, holding profile setting, RNA encoder, and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next experiment: it resolves the most consequential design decision—whether to invest further in multimodal configurations or focus on RNA-only improvements (aggregation, encoder choice). The result cleanly isolates the marginal contribution of the image modality in the multiprofile regime, and the answer will guide whether to explore the large multimodal configuration space (configs 019–051) or the smaller RNA-only space (configs 003–009) next."
}

